# End-of-Session Aider Review

At the **start of every session**, read `logs/aider_session_review.md`.

If the report contains `[BLOCKING]` items, address them before starting new feature work.
If it contains `[SHOULD FIX]` items, note them and factor them into the current session plan.

At the **end of every session** (or when the user says "we're done" / "end session"), remind the user to run:

```bash
bash scripts/aider_session_review.sh
```

This generates a fresh structural health report covering:
- Commit delta since last review
- Route file dependency correctness
- C0 / C1+ boundary violations
- Undocumented env vars or hardcoded secrets
- Dead code after route extractions
- Render deploy readiness

The report is saved to `logs/aider_session_review.md` and committed automatically by Aider.
